diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 5849f0b..1b75ff8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -22,6 +22,23 @@ It optionally depends on [Projectile](https://github.com/bbatsov/projectile) and
 
 Enable ActivityWatch for the current buffer by invoking `M-x activity-watch-mode`.  If you wish to activate it globally, run `M-x global-activity-watch-mode`.
 
+The watcher requires Emacs 27.1 or later. It records the selected buffer while
+its frame has known keyboard focus, including non-file buffers such as shells,
+chat clients and agent sessions. Background process buffers, unfocused frames,
+minibuffers and buffers with the minor mode disabled do not generate activity.
+Deferred mode initialization stays in the buffer that enabled it, so keyboard
+activity there resumes heartbeats after the idle timer stops them.
+
+Each heartbeat includes the buffer name (`buffer`) and its working directory
+(`cwd`), in addition to the existing `language`, `project`, `file` and `branch`
+fields. A non-file buffer has `file: "unknown"`. The directory is context, not
+proof of which project a chat conversation concerns. Project-name caching is
+invalidated when the working directory changes. Remote or missing directories
+retain their `cwd` but have unknown project and branch metadata.
+
+Buffer names and paths may contain private information. These fields are sent
+to the configured ActivityWatch server along with the existing file paths.
+
 
 ## Configuration
 
@@ -33,6 +50,15 @@ By default, the extension will try to infer the name of the project by consultin
 
 The default project name used when a proper one cannot be determined is "unknown" and can be customized via `activity-watch-project-name-default`.
 
+### Additional Buffer Context
+
+Add functions to `activity-watch-data-functions` to attach application-specific
+metadata. Each function runs in the sampled buffer with no arguments and returns
+an alist of additional JSON fields, or nil when not applicable. For example, a
+chat integration can return its actual channel and workspace identities. Use
+new field names; do not duplicate the built-in fields. These functions must read
+local metadata and should not perform network requests.
+
 ### Org-mode Integration (Optional)
 
 You can automatically link your tracked time to specific Org-mode tasks. When an Org clock is active, the watcher can inject a specific property from the clocked task into the ActivityWatch payload.
